---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const STORE = 'https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/umbra-browser-control-for/ccpcgfdklaihmikbpnnifegfonaojhli';
const shots = [
  { src: '/umbra/1-hero.webp', alt: 'a local agent driving Chrome from the terminal', caption: 'a local agent driving chrome from the terminal', lead: true },
  { src: '/umbra/5-terminal-mcp.webp', alt: 'MCP tool calls driving the browser', caption: 'MCP tool calls driving the browser' },
  { src: '/umbra/2-no-focus-theft.webp', alt: 'Umbra runs in the background without stealing focus', caption: 'runs in the background without stealing focus' },
  { src: '/umbra/3-tab-ownership.webp', alt: 'each session owns only the tabs it opened', caption: 'each session owns only the tabs it opened' },
  { src: '/umbra/4-options-local.webp', alt: 'local-only pairing on a key you generate', caption: 'local-only pairing on a key you generate' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Umbra"
  description="A Chrome extension that lets any LLM drive my signed-in browser, not just Claude in Chrome. Local, model-agnostic, no focus theft."
  currentSlug="umbra"
>
  <div class="readme">
    <p class="echo" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cwd">~/umbra</span><span class="chev"></span><span class="cmd">cat README.md</span></p>
    <h1 class="page-title">umbra</h1>
    <p class="lede">a chrome extension that lets any llm drive my signed-in browser, not just claude in chrome. pairs on a local key, runs in the background, nothing leaves the machine.</p>
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={STORE} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">get it on the chrome web store</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/RobertJLora/umbra" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">source on github</a>
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec-title">how it works</h2>
    <p>it's two pieces: a chrome extension that owns every browser action, and a small companion server on your machine that hands a browser tool surface to your mcp client.</p>
    <p>they talk over a websocket on <code>127.0.0.1</code>, signed with an hmac of a key you generate yourself.</p>

    <h2 class="sec-title">screenshots</h2>
    <div class="shots">
      {shots.map((s, i) => (
        <figure class:list={['shot', { 'shot-lead': s.lead }]}>
          <img src={s.src} alt={s.alt} width="1280" height="800" loading={i === 0 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>{s.caption}</figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2 class="sec-title">get it</h2>
    <p>install the extension from the <a href={STORE} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">chrome web store</a>, then set up the companion server:</p>
    <pre class="code"><code><span class="ln">git clone https://github.com/RobertJLora/umbra</span>
<span class="ln">cd umbra/mcp-server</span>
<span class="ln">npm install</span>
<span class="ln">node cli.js pair</span></code></pre>
    <p><code>pair</code> prints a key for the extension's options page and a config block for your mcp client. the full walkthrough is <a href="https://github.com/RobertJLora/umbra" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">on github</a>. the <a href="https://umbra-privacy.pages.dev">privacy details are here</a> (short version: it collects nothing).</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
